{
  "format": {
    "version": 1,
    "stage": "A",
    "owner": "level-designer",
    "summary": "Authored isometric floors (saved-layout format, GDD 5.15 / 11.3). Floor 15 is complete in Stage A; floors 13, 14, 16, 17 are TODO stubs with their intended unit lists for Stage B. All coordinates on this file are GLOBAL floor tiles (floor grid 30 x 22, section 5.3), unlike blueprints.json which is unit-local.",
    "grid": "floor = {w:30, d:22}. Tile (x,y), x 0-29 along the corridor, y 0-21 across; +x = screen lower right, +y = screen lower left (GDD section 2). Tile (x,y) covers [x,x+1) x [y,y+1).",
    "cells": "floor.rows = 22 strings (index = y) of 30 chars (index = x). Each char is a legend key. floor.legend maps a char to a roomId (or 'void'). Tile kinds: char '#' = VOID (not walkable, nothing drawn but wall faces); every other char = walkable FLOOR except stairs flights, which are STAIRS (listed in floor.stairwell). Several chars may map to the same roomId (the stairwell: 'N' landing, 'D' down flight, 'U' up flight are one room, so there is no wall between landing and flights).",
    "walls": "Walls are DERIVED, not listed: a WALL exists on every tile edge whose two sides have different roomIds (a void or the outside of the 30x22 grid counts as different). A doorway/door/window listed in floor.edges REPLACES the wall on that edge (kind DOOR or WINDOW). Everything else on a wall edge is plain wall. The elevator door and fire-door doorway are listed edges too (floor.edges.doorways).",
    "edges": "An edge entry = {id, x, y, side}: the edge of tile (x,y) on side N (toward -y, the edge at y), S (the edge at y+1), W (the edge at x), E (the edge at x+1). These are GRID sides, not screen compass. (x,y,E) and (x+1,y,W) are the same edge; entries use whichever tile is inside the unit. floor.edges.doors = {id, x, y, side, type:'front'|'interior', state:'open'|'closed'|'jammed', unit}. floor.edges.windows = {id, x, y, side, pane:true, curtains:bool} (every window carries a window_pane; pane=salvage 2 glass, becomes a window build spot when removed; curtains = a 'curtains' object on that edge). floor.edges.doorways = permanent openings without a door leaf ('fire_door_propped', 'elevator_door_dead').",
    "facing": "Facings N/E/S/W are GRID directions: N = toward -y (grid angle 270), E = +x (0), S = +y (90), W = -x (180). They are not the screen compass; the iso renderer maps grid 0/90/180/270 to its own sprite directions. Zombie and hero facings use the same letters, plus NE/SE/SW/NW as grid diagonals (none used in Stage A).",
    "rooms": "floor.rooms[roomId] = {type (templates room type), light: 'grey'|'dim'|'dark' (section 5.3 base light), unit}. roomId = f<floor><slot>.<ref name>.",
    "objects": "unit.objects[] = {id, objectId (balance.objects id, or 'workbench' fixture), tile:[x,y] first (min x, min y) footprint tile in GLOBAL coords, span:[w,h] (default [1,1]; footprint after orientation), facing N|E|S|W, layer 'floor'|'wall'|'corner', plus optional: mounted:true (hangs on the wall edge opposite its facing, tile stays free), fixture:true (workbench: Use only), fixedLoot:[{id,qty}] (first search gives exactly these, no table rolls), rolls:[min,max] (table rolls from the object's loot table, GDD 5.5; omitted on a non-container), empty:true (container is searched-out: shows an empty line), foundNote:{id,text} (paper card shown on the first search)}. Containers with neither fixedLoot nor rolls use the 0-2 default rolls. Ids follow the GDD: f<floor><slot>-<x>.<y> with the unit-LOCAL tile after mirroring of the footprint origin (NE: x-18; SW: y-12; SE: x-18 and y-12; S: x-12 and y-12; NW: x,y).",
    "zombies": "unit.zombies[] = {id, type:'crawler'|'walker', tile:[x,y], facing, room: roomId}. Fair-encounter rules (GDD 5.4) are enforced in the data: the first room behind a front door never holds a walker; no zombie within 2 tiles of a front door; walkers face away from where the hero enters; max 1 zombie per tile.",
    "survivors": "unit.survivors[] = [] (none on floor 15; Mara is Stage B on floor 13).",
    "scriptedSpawns": "floor.scriptedSpawns[] = {id, type, tile, facing, trigger}: spawned when the trigger fires. Floor 15: the tutorial crawler in the corridor just outside the start flat's front door, trigger 'tutorial_open_door' (tutorial is OFF in Stage A: do not spawn).",
    "stairwell": "floor.stairwell = {downFlight:{tiles, landingEnd}, upFlight:{tiles, landingEnd}, elevatorShaft (void), landing, doorway (propped fire door), elevatorDoor, floorNumber (decor edge for the stencil), blocked:{up,down,thought}}. Tapping any flight tile walks to its landingEnd tile then climbs (section 5.3). Stage A: both flights blocked with the thought 'The stairs are blocked.'.",
    "home": "floor.home = {unit, heroStart:{tile,facing}, bed (object id), workbench (object id), stash:{tile,slots}, frontDoor (door id), barricadeSpot:{x,y,side}}. unit.buildSpots = {floor:[{id,tile,requiresEmpty?}], window:[window edge ids that can take a window build once the pane is removed], barricade:{x,y,side}}. A floor spot with requiresEmpty is only usable after the object on that tile is dismantled.",
    "units": "floor.units[] = {id (f<floor><slot>), slot, template, blueprint (blueprints.json id), mirror:[x,y], rect:[x,y,w,h] in global tiles, name, flavour, condition 'normal'|'ransacked'|'burned', home?:true, objects, zombies, survivors, buildSpots?}. Unit doors/windows are in floor.edges, tagged with unit.",
    "stubs": "A floor with status 'TODO_stage_B' has only number, purpose, difficulty, expectedMinutes and planned[] (slot, template, name, condition, front door state, what it holds) taken from docs/LEVELS.md; Stage B turns it into the same structure as floor 15.",
    "lightNotes": "Windowless dim rooms: hallway, bathroom, corridor middle, landing. The corridor's 3 end tiles on each side are Grey (grid.corridorWindowGreyTiles); the engine derives that from the corridor end windows."
  },
